AB  - In the above-named article by Rosenberg EA and Seely EW (J Clin Endo Metab. 2023; doi: 10.1210/clinem/dgad600), there were typographical errors within the article: In Table 1, under the column “Pregnancy outcome/reproductive risk factors,” “GD” has been corrected to read “GDM.” In the abbreviations of Table 1, “GD” has been corrected to read “GDM.” In Table 3, under the column “Definition,” in the “Preeclampsia” row, “New onset hypertension (systolic blood pressure ≥140 mmHg and/or diastolic blood pressure ≥90 mmHg) at ≥20 weeks of gestation without proteinuria or new signs of end-organ dysfunctiona” has been corrected to read “New onset hypertension (systolic blood pressure ≥140 mmHg and/or diastolic blood pressure ≥90 mmHg) at ≥20 weeks of gestationa.” “New onset hypertension (systolic blood pressure ≥160 mmHg and/or diastolic blood pressure ≥110 mmHg)b” has been corrected to read “New onset hypertension (systolic blood pressure ≥160 mmHg and/or diastolic blood pressure ≥110 mmHg) at ≥20 weeks of gestationb.” “Proteinuria (300 mg/24 hour urine, protein/Cr ratio 0.3, dipstick reading 2 + protein)” has been corrected to read “Proteinuria (≥300 mg/24 hour urine, or protein/Cr ratio ≥ 0.3, or dipstick reading ≥2 + protein).” “Thrombocytopenia (platelet count less than 100 000)” has been corrected to read “Thrombocytopenia (platelet count < 100 000 /microL).” “Renal insufficiency (serum Cr >1.1 mg/dL or doubling of the serum Cr)” has been corrected to read “Renal insufficiency (serum Cr >1.1 mg/dL or doubling of the serum Cr in the absence of other kidney disease).” In Table 3, under the column “Definition,” in the “Severe features of hypertensive disorders of pregnancy” row, “Severe features of hypertensive disorders of pregnancy” has been corrected to read “Severe features of hypertensive disorders of pregnancyc.” The following text has been added to the footnotes of the table, “cIn an individual with preeclampsia, the presence of one or more severe features designates a diagnosis of “preeclampsia with severe features.” “Thrombocytopenia (platelet count less than 100 000)” has been corrected to read “Thrombocytopenia (platelet count < 100 000 /microL).” “Renal insufficiency (serum Cr >1.1 mg/dL or doubling of the serum Cr)” has been corrected to read “Renal insufficiency (serum Cr >1.1 mg/dL or doubling of the serum Cr in the absence of other kidney disease).” “Visual symptoms” has been corrected to read “Visual disturbance.” The article has been corrected online. doi: 10.1210/clinem/dgad600. © The Author(s) 2023.
