TI  - Prognostic Modeling of Diabetes Mellitus in Women: A comparitive analysis of Machine Learning algorithms integrating Clinical and Genetic Data
PY  - 2024
T2  - International Conference on Emerging Technologies in Computer Science for Interdisciplinary Applications, ICETCS 2024
DO  - 10.1109/ICETCS61022.2024.10544284
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85196109919&doi=10.1109%2fICETCS61022.2024.10544284&partnerID=40&md5=dfc82e3d1edeb180c6d626125fa6989c
AB  - Diabetes is considered as one of the most commonly observed medical condition among human beings. Millions of people worldwide are affected by a chronic condition that goes by the name of diabetes. There are 3 sorts of diabetes and they comprise of Type 1, Type 2 and Gestational diabetes. Early prediction of diabetes helps to avoid complications like diabetic retinopathy which leads to blindness. There is a 13% higher risk of death among people with diabetes, especially in women, cardiovascular disease caused by diabetes attributes to 50% higher risk of death, coronary heart disease caused by diabetes contributes to a 58% higher risk of death. The proposed research work aims in predicting diabetes from the symptoms a patient exhibit. The proposed system is a healthcare assisting system which is accessible to patients as well as medical practitioners. The system is developed as a web application using the features of Django python framework along with suitable database management system. The system is powered with gradient boosting machine learning algorithm for predictions. By using the web application along with a blood test to find out the insulin levels and glucose levels in blood, any user can predict whether he/she would be affected by diabetes in future and can avoid the complications caused by diabetes. © 2024 IEEE.
