AB  - Declaration of Competing Interest statements were not included in the published version of the following articles that appeared in previous issues of Obesity Medicine. The appropriate Declaration/Competing Interest statements, provided by the Authors, are included below. 1. “Optimal dosage of vitamin D supplementation in obese patients with low serum levels of 25-Hydroxyvitamin D. A systematic review” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 29: 100381] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2021.100381Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 2. “Comparison of Foeniculum Vulgare versus metformin on insulin resistance and anthropometric indices of women with polycystic ovary, an open-label controlled trial study” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 31: 100401] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2022.100401Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 3. “Identifying overnutrition risk groups in Bangladeshi married women based on sociodemographic factors: A classification and regression tree model” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 33: 100425] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2022.100425Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 4. “Predictors of online vs. in-person preference for lifestyle change programs among women with a history of gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM)” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 33: 100424] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2022.100424Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 5. “The effect of 12 weeks aerobic, resistance and combined trainings on peripheral vascular disease in type 2 diabetes with peripheral neuropathy in men” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 34: 100439] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2022.100439Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 6. “Prevalence and knowledge of cardiovascular disease risk factors among young adults in Saudi Arabia” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 36: 100457] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2022.100457Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 7. “A retrospective study assessing the effects of bariatric surgery on comorbid conditions and quality of life in obese individuals” [Obesity Medicine, 2023; 38: 100479] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2023.100479Declaration of competing interest: The Authors have no interests to declare. 8. “Body weight and prandial variation of plasma metabolites in subjects undergoing gastric band-induced weight loss” [Obesity Medicine, 2022; 33: 100434] https://doi.org/10.1016/j.obmed.2022.100434Declaration of competing interest: The authors declare the following financial interests/personal relationships which may be considered as potential competing interests: Dr. José O. Alemán is a Consultant for Novo Nordisk; Clinical Advisor and Consultant for Intellihealth. © 2023
