TI  - Dumping syndrome after bariatric surgery in a pregnant woman: A case report
PY  - 2023
T2  - Malaysian Family Physician
VL  - 18
C7  - 24
DO  - 10.51866/cr.257
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85168483535&doi=10.51866%2fcr.257&partnerID=40&md5=38ccc42a4f69c8b4f94c53b0435eabc8
AB  - Dumping syndrome after bariatric surgery is common. However, it is rarely seen during pregnancy because patients are usually advised to avoid pregnancy immediately after surgery. This case highlights the importance of avoidance of pregnancy after bariatric surgery. We report a case of unplanned pregnancy in a 35-year-old woman with a history of subfertility for 8 years who conceived spontaneously 3 months after gastric bypass surgery. This occurred because there was no contraception offered to her after the procedure. The pregnancy was complicated with recurrent episodes of hypoglycaemia secondary to dumping syndrome. Primary care providers need to be vigilant and have a high index of suspicion for dumping syndrome in pregnant obese women who have undergone bariatric surgery. © 2023, Academy of Family Physicians of Malaysia. All rights reserved.
