TI  - Current Practice and Controversies in Screening for Gestational Diabetes
PY  - 2023
T2  - Current Diabetes Reviews
VL  - 19
IS  - 2
C7  - e130622205912
DO  - 10.2174/1573399819666220613154802
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85150211698&doi=10.2174%2f1573399819666220613154802&partnerID=40&md5=34ee4af54d68d52f3bff9b55d0bcb582
AB  - Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) is associated with fetal and maternal complica-tions, and the prevalence has been increasing over the past decades. Hence, it is imperative to effectively screen, manage and monitor patients with GDM, but there continues to be a lack of consensus on optimal screening for GDM internationally. In this review, we discuss the current screening methods for GDM, some of which are controversial and vary across several different healthcare systems. We also discuss the changes adapted to these guidelines during the COVID-19 pandemic and review novel approaches to the screening of GDM. © 2023 Bentham Science Publishers.
