AB  - Overt diabetes mellitus during pregnancy is associated with substantial adverse outcomes both for maternal and neonatal health. Women with gestational diabetes face an increased risk for future development of dysglycemia and cardiovascular disease, both related to serious comorbidities and reduced life expectancy. Strategies for long-term follow-up combined with lifestyle modification and pharmacological interventions aim to regulate specific cardiovascular factors and improve maternal outcomes. This chapter explores the long-term maternal complications in women with a history of gestational diabetes, reviews the current guidelines and recommendations for screening and interpretation of glucose monitoring, and outlines postpartum care strategies to prevent or delay the development of type 2 diabetes. © The Editor(s) (if applicable) and The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2022.
