AB  - Gestational diabetes mellitus (GDM) has an increased risk of adverse pregnancy outcomes. The incidence rate of macrosomia, chronic intrauterine hypoxia, fetal heart dysfunction and malformation of GDM fetuses were much higher than that of non-diabetic pregnancy. The progresses of prenatal ultrasonography for predicting adverse pregnancy outcomes caused by GDM were reviewed in this article. Copyright © 2021 by the Press of Chinese Journal of Medical Imaging and Technology.
