AB  - Diabetes is a group of chronic metabolic diseases in which blood sugar levels are increased. There are different types of diabetes i.e., type 1 diabetes, type 2 diabetes, gestational diabetes, and other specific type (monogenic diabetes). The prevalence of diabetes is increasing glob-ally with more socioeconomic consequences; therefore, high blood sugar creates the symptoms of frequent urination, increased thirst, and increased hunger. Untreated, diabetes causes many complications; acute complications include diabetic ketoacidosis, serious complications include heart disease, stroke, kidney failure, foot ulcers, and retinopathy. In diabetic condition the pancreas do not produce enough amount of insulin, or the pancreatic cells do not respond properly to the insulin produced by the body. There are many pharmacological treatments available for the management of hyperglycemia, but recently there are advance treatments available like stem cells therapy, gene therapy, diabetes vaccine etc. Stem cell therapy is one of the emerging treatments for diabetes. Stem cells help in pancreatic regeneration, also increase the functioning of β-cells, angiogenesis, and immunomodulation and hence maintain normal blood sugar level in diabetics. © Nova Science Publishers, Inc.
