AB  - Children born to a diabetic mother face some nutritional problems staring from the neonatal period to childhood. Hypoglycemia is one of the most frequent complications for a baby in a diabetic mother. Although breastfeeding is essential, formulas are sometimes needed. Obesity, metabolic syndrome, diabetes mellitus, and cardiovascular diseases are the longterm complications related to nutrition. © 2020 by Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.
