UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85148811523&partnerID=40&md5=c940357866458dc9f2a217590aa169aa
AB  - Gestational diabetes is defined as carbohydrate intolerance of any degree with onset or first recognition during pregnancy. It is the most commonly observed endocrine disorder during pregnancy, making it a high-risk pregnancy with maternal, fetal, and neonatal complications. Diabetic women have a markedly higher risk for a number of pregnancy complications, including spontaneous abortion, preterm birth, polyhydramnios and hypertensive disorder. However, once the major issue is addressed - namely, that the diagnosis of GDM is thought to be associated with a high risk of developing diabetes, obesity and cardiovascular disease in later life - efforts should be made to prevent or ameliorate the emergence of these complications. © 2020 by Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.
