TI  - Management of monochorionic monoamniotic twins: Case reports and a review of literatures
PY  - 2018
T2  - Clinical and Experimental Obstetrics and Gynecology
VL  - 45
IS  - 6
SP  - 910
EP  - 912
DO  - 10.12891/ceog4350.2018
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85058851320&doi=10.12891%2fceog4350.2018&partnerID=40&md5=dd1b07df53e68f0e19841813abd6340b
AB  - Monochorionic monoamniotic (MCMA) twins are rare but are associated with higher morbidity and mortality rates than monochorionic diamniotic (MCDA) twins. Although the prenatal prognosis of MCMA pregnancy has improved with advanced prenatal care, no consensus has been reached for the management for MCMA twins. Here, the authors report two cases of MCMA twin pregnancies diagnosed at 30 weeks of gestation and complicated with congenital heart disease, respectively, with a review of literature on MCMA twin pregnancies. © 2018 S.O.G. Canada Inc.All rights reserved.
