VL  - 15
IS  - 6
SP  - 56
EP  - 64
DO  - 10.17116/rosakush201515656-64
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85030861628&doi=10.17116%2frosakush201515656-64&partnerID=40&md5=d7f17631ebb1d9c8b4d51868646d49cb
AB  - Objective — to optimize pregnancy and delivery management tactics in female patients with cerebral arteriovenous malforma-tion. Subject and methods. The course of pregnancy and labor and perinatal outcomes were retrospectively and prospectively analyzed in 17 pregnant women with cerebral arteriovenous malformation. All the patients underwent conventional clinical and laboratory examinations, hemostatic system study, thrombophilia screening, and instrumental studies of the central nervous system, such as computed tomography, magnetic resonance imaging, and electroencephalography. All the patients were exam-ined by a neurosurgeon, a neurologist, an oculist, and an anesthetist who together created a pregnancy and labor management plan. Results. Surgical treatment was performed in 7 patients with hemorrhagic stroke and in 3 patients with cerebral arteriove-nous malformation before the current pregnancy. The latter was accompanied by gestational complications (pernicious vomiting, threatened miscarriage, fetoplacental insufficiency, moderate preeclampsia, and gestational diabetes mellitus). Cesarean section was the delivery method of choice (70.6%). The status of all the neonates, but one who had been born with congenital malformation (spina bifida), was satisfactory. The postpartum follow-up of all the patients lasted 5 years. There were no cases of progressive neurological symptomatology. Conclusion. This cohort of pregnant women is a group at high risk for severe obstetric complications and possible intracranial hemorrhage particularly when there are pregnancy-specific circulating blood volume increases and hemostatic changes. These patients should be jointly managed by obstetricians/gynecologists, neurosurgeons, anesthetists, and neuroresuscitators. A delivery mode should be also chosen jointly. © 2015, Media Sphera Publishing Group. All rights reserved.
