TI  - Exercise training before surgical revascularisation-influence on short term outcomes
PY  - 2015
T2  - JK Practitioner
VL  - 20
IS  - 1-2
SP  - 21
EP  - 24
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84930367720&partnerID=40&md5=d93b340c5e0b773bfbb4029ace618205
AB  - Cardiovascular rehabilitation (CVR) is usually not performed or is interrupted before coronary artery By-pass graft (CABG) interventions. To assess the influence of exercise training prior to surgery on perioperative complications and short term prognosis. We studied 106 patients (P), all included in rehabilitation programs in a specialized clinic. Over a period of 8 years progression of coronary heart disease (CHD) led to indication for CABG. The events leading to CABG indications were reappearance of anginal episodes (61) and/or subclinical heart failure, newly detected by echocardiography and BNP levels. Patients with more than 1,5 fold increase of cardiac necrosis enzymes were excluded. The control group (Co) consisted of 66P who interrupted CVR 6wk. to 6 mo. prior to surgery. The study group (St) consisted of 40 P who continued mild exercise similar to phase I and II post acute myocardial infarction. Except for gender differences (more females in Co, p=0,03) the groups were matched in starting parameters. We followed perioperative complications, ICU stay, hospitalization period, mortality and CHD complications at a 6 mo. follow up, before engaging in phase III CVR. The study group showed significant decrease in thromboembolic events (p<0,01), depression scores (p<0,01) and respiratory complications (p=0,03), leading to fewer complications during hospital stay (p=0,02) and shorter ICU stay (p=0,02). Effort capacity was better in the study group at discharge (6 MWT, p<0,01). However, at 6 mo. follow up these advantages disappeared, with no differences in mortality, CHD complications or effort capacity. Exercise training was safe before CABG, led to decreased perioperative complications, shorter hospital stay, lowering costs. However, no clear benefit was noted anymore at 6 months. © 2015 JK-Practitioner.
