AB  - Currently, epidemiological, clinical and experimental data are being intensively discussed which indicate that exposures during prenatal and perinatal life have lifelong consequences for the risk of developing chronic diseases like obesity, diabetes and cardiovascular diseases. This paper reviews current knowledge on mechanisms which might underlie processes of programming, focussing on perinatal programming of the regulation of body weight and metabolism. Using the example of gestational diabetes and its long-term consequences for risk of obesity and diabetes in the offspring, the potentially far-ranging consequences of being aware of such mechanisms are discussed. © 2007 Springer Medizin Verlag.
