TI  - Awareness status of type 2 diabetes mellitus and its influencing factors among residents in the community of cigarette factory
PY  - 2005
T2  - Chinese Journal of Clinical Rehabilitation
VL  - 9
IS  - 23
SP  - 16
EP  - 17
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-27644454705&partnerID=40&md5=580de2c6238bb55b792707835f8f48b2
AB  - Aim: To investigate the awareness rate and the awareness of the knowledge of type 2 diabetes mellitus and the related influencing factors among the residents in the community of cigarette factory. Methods: An epidemiological survey about diabetes mellitus was applied to 1850 residents above 40 years old in the community of Zhengzhou Cigarette General Factory between June and July 2003, all the subjects took part in this survey voluntarily. They were surveyed by means of questionnaire with cluster sampling, totally 1 789 cases (738 males and 1 051 females) aged 40 to 88 years filled in the questionnaire with concrete contents. The surveyed contents included the awareness of type 2 diabetes mellitus and its complications (hypertension, coronary heart disease, oculopathy and nephritic syndrome), and knowledge related to diabetes mellitus, the subjects should answer "yes" or "no", and then the scores were added up (1 point for each question with right answer). The diagnostic criteria for type 2 diabetes mellitus set by WHO in 1999 was used, that was, fasting blood glucose ≥ 7.0 mmol/L, oral glucose tolerance test 2-hour blood glucose ≥11.1 mmol/L; Those with type 1 diabetes mellitus, other specific diabetes and gestational diabetes mellitus. The data were analyzed with χ2 test and χ2 test for trends. Results: A total of 1 789 concretely filled questionnaires were collected, the 61 deleted ones were all filled incompletely or different from the reality. 1 The awareness rate of diabetes mellitus among the residents in the community of cigarette factory was only 57.14%. 2 The awareness rate of type 2 diabetes mellitus was higher in the residents below 60 years old than in those above 60 years old (62.59%, 50.00%, χ2=3.87, P < 0.05), higher in males than in females (66.67%, 54.68%, χ2=3.87, P < 0.05), also higher in those with higher educational background and better economic status than in other crowds (χ2trend=5.14,4.16, P < 0.05), higher in medical staff than those involved in other professions (66.67%, 56.90%, χ2=4.00,P < 0.05). 3 The awareness of the knowledge related to type 2 diabetes mellitus was superior in the residents below 60 years old than in those above 60 years old (χ2=4.45, P < 0.05), higher in males than in females (χ2=6.31, P < 0.05), also higher in those with higher educational background and better economic status than in other crowds (χ2trend=58.91, 13.06, P < 0.01), higher in medical staff than those involved in other professions (χ2=22.11, P < 0.01). 4 The awareness of type 2 diabetic patients had significant differences in the time of the latest measurement of blood glucose (χ2trend=109.06, P < 0.01). The consciousness of blood glucose self-surveillance was better in males than in the females (χ2=14.19, P < 0.01), better in the residents below 60 years than in those above 60 years old (χ2=9.68, P < 0.05), also better in the residents with higher monthly income than in those with lower one (χ2trend=4.26, P < 0.05). Conclusion: The awareness rate of diabetes mellitus among residents in the community of cigarette factory is lower, Age, gender, occupation, educational background, income status and blood sugar self-surveillance are the main factors that affect the awareness of type 2 diabetes mellitus and the related knowledge. So the health education of the knowledge related to diabetes mellitus to the diabetic patients should be taken as the key point for the prevention and treatment of community medical service.
