UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-33750248076&partnerID=40&md5=e1471e4c109778888d5f1534af8a1177
AB  - The present eommunication demonstrates that in streptoJ.olocininduced diabetic rats, the concentrations of serum total cholesterol and triacylglycerol were significantly increased whereas the concentration of HDL-cholestcrol was significantly decreased. These changes in serum lipids were adjusted with the administration of insulin to diabetic rats as these values became nearly similar to those of control rats. Results of streptozolocin-induced diabetic pregnant rats showed a significant increase in serum total cholesterol concentration only in the third trimester, whereas the concentration of serum triacylclyccrol was significantly increased throughout the period of pregnancy. However, the concentration of serum HDL-cholesterol was significantly decreased throughout pregnancy when compared with non-diabetic pregnant rats. It is therefore concluded that uncontrolled diabetes or gestational diabetes can well be regarded as a secondary factor for atherosclerosis.
